  m_Name: Lesson_L1_ChordTones
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Jazztures.Lessons::Jazztures.Lessons.LessonDefinition
  _id: L1
  _title: Chord tones
  _menuDescription: Play notes with your right hand. Curl a finger as each letter
    arrives.
  _conceptExplanation: 
  _conceptSlides:
  - text: A chord is several notes played together. The notes that belong to a chord
      are called chord tones.
    seconds: 8
  - text: In this lesson your right hand plays chord tones.
    seconds: 5
  - text: You'll see a line attached to each of your fingers.
    seconds: 4
  - text: Letters slide down the lines toward you. Each letter is the name of a note.
    seconds: 7
  - text: When a note reaches your fingertip, curl that finger to play the note.
    seconds: 7
  - text: A chord plays underneath on its own. Time your finger curls to hit the
      notes.
    seconds: 7
